#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
p5_coefleg_verify -- independent re-derivation of the four claims in
output/evidence/p5_coefleg.json.

Deliberately different numerical routes from the original package:
  * arrays are reconstructed by sorting + reshape (not pivot_table), and the two
    routes are cross-checked against each other;
  * the associated Legendre functions are generated by an explicit recurrence
    (no-CS convention) and cross-checked against scipy.special.lpmv;
  * the "affine R2" is evaluated with numpy.polyfit and additionally identified
    analytically as the squared Pearson correlation;
  * the DME greedy leave-one-out scan is done in closed form from centred
    Gram/cross-product matrices instead of repeated lstsq calls;
  * the dense-panel reference for the six off-grid energies is taken both as the
    original nearest panel AND as the linear interpolation between the two
    bracketing 0.1 eV panels;
  * extra harsher tests: ridge LOO with GCV-selected alpha on the full 105-feature
    dictionary, energy-only LOO with a cubic, Spearman selection, energy-block
    permutation nulls.

Writes: output/evidence/p5_coefleg_verdict.json
Appends stdout to: output/evidence/p5_coefleg_verify.log
"""

